        "evidence": [
          "All six moved files are exact git-object matches, not merely equal content: `cat-file -p base_tree:openspec/changes/deterministic-verification-evidence` lists design.md as blob fc4a353d, proposal.md as blob 7a00f47e, specs/ as tree 3c698e18, tasks.md as blob efae9589; `cat-file -p candidate_tree:openspec/changes/archive/2026-08-05-deterministic-verification-evidence` lists the identical four object hashes plus one new blob (archive-report.md, 495539da) — proving a true move with zero re-serialization risk. `cat-file -p candidate_tree:openspec/changes/deterministic-verification-evidence` returns 'fatal: path ... does not exist', confirming the source directory was fully and cleanly removed with no orphaned files. sha256/cmp on extracted blobs confirm byte counts base==archived: design.md 8916B, proposal.md 4453B, tasks.md 41800B (not the previously-seen 519B truncation), deterministic-check-runner/spec.md 3964B, deterministic-verification-policy/spec.md 4159B, verification-evidence-capture/spec.md 7623B — matching the archive report's byte table exactly. Each of the three openspec/specs/\u003ccapability\u003e/spec.md promoted files is byte-for-byte identical (cmp, sha256) to its corresponding delta spec, and `cat-file -p base_tree:openspec/specs/\u003ccapability\u003e/spec.md` errors 'exists on disk, but not in \u003cbase_tree\u003e' for all three, confirming no pre-existing canonical spec was silently overwritten (consistent with their A, not M, status in the manifest). `### Requirement:` heading counts in the promoted specs are 6, 6, 7 = 19, matching the archive report's claimed total exactly. tasks.md contains exactly 82 '- [x]' lines and zero '- [ ]' lines, confirming the claimed 82/82 completion. The manifest's 16 entries reconcile with no orphans: 6 deletions pair 1:1 with 6 archived files, the 7th archive-folder addition (archive-report.md) is legitimately new, and the 3 openspec/specs/ additions are the promotions. Claims outside the frozen trees —